If PC1 wants to send data to PC3, how would it be done, since it knows only its IP address, but switches only know MAC address. The first step is to use ARP, which is used to 
discover a layer 2 address (used by switches) when we know a layer 3 address. PC1 would then send an ARP request (broadcast, meaning the destination MAC is FFFF.FFFF.FFFF) to
SW1. SW1 learns PC1 MAC address (dynamic MAC address) and bradcast the ARP request to all its interfaces (except the PC1 one). PC2 receives it and ignores it, SW2 receives it,
learns PC1 MAC address and broadcasts it to all its interfaces. PC4 ignores it and PC3 reply with an ARP Reply, but this time, no boradcast will be needed since it knows the 
MAC of PC1. Once PC1 receives the ARP Reply, it then sens the data.

